      "side": 1,
      "message": "A little scary.  If the caller does \u0027usb updater -i 0x%x:0x%x\u0027, then something like 0x42 will be interpreted as a string.\n\nFrom a security standpoint that\u0027s ok, as long as valid RLZ codes don\u0027t start with \"0x\" and don\u0027t contain \":\".  But it could still cause some confusion.\n\nIs there some other relatively painless way to differentiate strings from numeric IDs?",
